{
  "title": "AWS in 3D: an event-driven write path",
  "view": "iso",
  "description": "An API Gateway call triggers a Lambda that writes to DynamoDB. Failed events go to a dead-letter queue. On the layer below, a table stream feeds an indexer that keeps OpenSearch up to date.",
